  "id": "Compound::DB00393 - Gene::784",
  "verbalization": "Nimodipine is implicated in the regulation of high voltage-gated calcium channel activity through its interaction with Cacna1f and Cacna1s, which are subunits of the calcium channel complex. These interactions are supported by the observed binding of Nimodipine to these proteins and their role in modulating calcium channel function. The evidence suggests that Nimodipine may influence Cacnb3 through a shared pathway involving calcium channel activity, as Cacnb3 is a participant in this process. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Nimodipine could modulate calcium channel activity, potentially affecting cellular processes related to calcium homeostasis. The consistent involvement of Cacnb3 in the high voltage-gated calcium channel activity pathway, coupled with the binding of Nimodipine to related proteins, supports a role for Nimodipine in regulating this activity.",
